{
  "note": "The Avinguda Meridiana's cross-section after the 2025-26 works (Felip II–Fabra i Puig phase), drawn by hand over the OpenStreetMap data (osm.json) from OSM's own carriageways, the city's design and photos taken on the avenue in October 2026: the 10 m east sidewalk, its kerb bed with young trees (paved through at the Fabra i Puig bus stop), the east carriageway (two lanes and the bus lane by the kerb, towards Fabra i Puig), the planted median with the two-way bike lane between two beds, the west carriageway (two lanes and the bus lane, towards Hipercor) and the west bed. Beds stop at the three zebras, where people cross on panot. East of the Escòcia crossing the avenue turns about 1.4° (OSM's carriageways drift some 7 m by Meridiana 335), so every bed and carriageway bends there. In the turned frame: metres, x along the avenue (+x towards Fabra i Puig, north-west), z across it (+z towards the camera: the even side, Hipercor's). zone.json `redraw` leaves OSM's own Meridiana ways out. At the east edge (features `revolt-*`) the avenue starts to bend north-west round Plaça de Josep Benet i Morell.",
